 ## Usage
 
+One command, if you just want the number:
+
+```bash
+python -m groundhog bench /path/to/repo --agent claude-code
+```
+
+That mines, validates, races and reports into `.groundhog/<repo>/`, skipping any
+stage whose file is already there — so re-running it races again without
+re-mining, `--resume` finishes an interrupted race, and `--fresh` starts over.
+
+The same thing as four commands, which is what you want as soon as you care
+about the files in between:
+
 ```bash
 python -m groundhog mine     /path/to/repo --since "6 months ago"
 python -m groundhog validate /path/to/repo
